====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|informal|ambitransitive}} To [[represent]]; to act as a representative for.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1922|author=Hal G. Evarts|title=The Settling of the Sage|chapter=|edition=|url=http://www.gutenberg.org/etext/18856
|passage=Bentley, the man who '''repped''' for Slade, carried the air and the rest joined in.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=November 4, 1994|author=Bill Wyman|title=Evanston's New Music Hall/Veruca Salt Grow Up/Schmitsville|work=Chicago Reader|url=https://securesite.chireader.com/cgi-bin/Archive/abridged2.bat?path=1994/941104/HITSV
|passage=He left to help the Reader set up its national advertising arm, went back to Rolling Stone for five years, '''repped''' other magazines, and finally set up his own company, which currently scouts ads for the Atlantic, Spin, Discover, and a publication called Disney Adventures.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} To display as a representative example.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2023-03-03|author=Natasha Harding|title=Olivia Rodrigo's leather boob tube will transport you back to 2001|journal={{w|Cosmopolitan (journal)|Cosmopolitan}}|url=https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/fashion/celebrity/a43173962/olivia-rodrigo-billboard-women-in-music-outfit/|passage=Last year, Olivia famously went full-2000s at a Grammys after-party she attended with Paris Hilton, where she '''repped''' a bright blue butterfly dress featuring a plunging neckline and dramatic ruffles. Now, for her latest look, she's gone and '''repped''' another recognisable combination: silk trousers and a leather boob tube.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261009022617/https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/fashion/celebrity/a43173962/olivia-rodrigo-billboard-women-in-music-outfit/|archivedate=9 October 2026}}
# {{lb|en|knitting|crochet}} {{abbr of|en|repeat}}.
#* {{RQ:Guardian|title=How to make colourful crocheted flowers|author=Carmen Heffernan|date=August 23 2011
|text='''Rep''' from * to * 6 times. Fasten off.
|url=https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2011/aug/23/how-to-make-crocheted-flowers|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20231224163400/https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2011/aug/23/how-to-make-crocheted-flowers}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|weightlifting}} To [[lift]] for multiple reps.
#: {{rfex|en}}

===Etymology 2===
{{back-form|en|reps}}, misinterpreted as a plural.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|repp}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|textiles}} A fabric made of silk or wool, or of silk and wool, and having a transversely corded or ribbed surface. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
#* {{RQ:Lindsay Redheap|page=60|passage=It was decorated in {{...}} horsehair and red '''rep''' curtains[.]}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|author=Amy X. Wang; Grant Cornett|title=Inside the Delirious Rise of ‘Superfake’ Handbags|date=2023-05-04|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/05/04/magazine/celine-chanel-gucci-superfake-handbags.html|passage=I toted a (rather fetching) $100 Gucci 1955 Horsebit '''rep''' through a vacation across Europe {{...}}|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260102010244/https://www.nytimes.com/2023/05/04/magazine/celine-chanel-gucci-superfake-handbags.html|archivedate=2 January 2026}}

